snippet.textDisplay:
@Themix274 I understand what you’re saying, but this is even on another level than smartphones. Most people when they use their smartphones, are both passive and predictable. Open the same apps, text the same people, read the same topics, etc.

Giving these robots the ability to move through a physical space (a home, office, street, etc) changes things. The robots will be able to analyze body language and routines that a phone simply won’t be able to analyze.

If I had to sum it up, Smartphones watch what you do on them and may listen to your conversation if it’s left in the same room.  Humanoid robots will be watching what you do in real life, while your on your phone and for the time your away from your phone.

